(A list field given to a value parameter beside an `each` clause is copied
 for every call, so each call sees the field as it was when it was made.)
A thing called note has
  a list called items.

a note called memo.
append "a" to memo's items.

To 'look' with a value called kept and a number called round.
    append "b" to memo's items.
    Print "round {round} kept: {kept}".

'look' of memo's items and each round from [1, 2].
Print "memo: {memo's items}".
